# LIQUID-07 — Avoid passing whole objects to snippets

## Rationale

Passing entire objects to `{% render %}` increases processing overhead, reduces
caching efficiency, and ties snippets to specific object shapes. Pass only the
primitive values the snippet needs.

## How to check

```bash
bun "<skill-dir>/scripts/cli.ts" check liquid-performance <file>
```

Flags `{% render %}` calls that pass `variant:`, `product:`, `collection:`, etc.

## How to fix

List the properties the snippet reads and pass them as individual arguments.

## Examples

### Bad

```liquid
{% for variant in product.variants %}
  {% render 'price-display', variant: variant %}
{% endfor %}
```

```liquid
{% comment %} snippets/price-display.liquid {% endcomment %}
{% if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price %}
  <span class="price-sale">{{ variant.price | money }}</span>
{% endif %}
```

### Good

```liquid
{% for variant in product.variants %}
  {% render 'price-display',
      price: variant.price,
      compare_at_price: variant.compare_at_price %}
{% endfor %}
```

```liquid
{% comment %} snippets/price-display.liquid {% endcomment %}
{% if compare_at_price and compare_at_price > price %}
  <span class="price-sale">{{ price | money }}</span>
  <span class="price-compare">{{ compare_at_price | money }}</span>
{% endif %}
```
